       "html": "<p><strong>Why:</strong> Every future video needs cutaway shots of the app actually doing things. Recording them once, labeled, means editors (usually Avinaya in CapCut) grab clips instead of scheduling re-shoots.\n<strong>Where:</strong> Buzzend on your Android device, using the built-in screen recorder.\n<strong>Tools:</strong> Android phone, Do Not Disturb ON, shared drive, tracker.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Prep the phone so nothing personal leaks into footage: Do Not Disturb on, notifications cleared, battery above 50%, a clean profile name in the app (remember the public-imagery rule — raw personal screens never go out; these clips get cut into edits, so record them clean).</li>\n<li>Record these flows as separate clips, 10–20 seconds each, in this order: (1) create a challenge, (2) invite a friend, (3) join a challenge with a code, (4) leaderboard with live standings, (5) a Beat-It attempt flow, (6) the streak screen with the flame, (7) the discover page of trending challenges, (8) daily goal completing, (9) the rep-counter counting a short real set (prop the phone, do the reps — never a faked count), (10) the workout summary screen.</li>\n<li>Name every file the same way: <code>broll-01-challenge-create.mp4</code>, <code>broll-02-invite.mp4</code>, … <code>broll-10-summary.mp4</code>. Re-record any clip with stutter or a mis-tap — 10 clean clips beats 15 messy ones.</li>\n<li>Upload the folder to the shared drive.</li>\n<li>In the tracker, add one row per clip: filename · what it shows · length · date. This list is what Avinaya and Riya will search, so write the &quot;what it shows&quot; column for someone who hasn&#39;t seen the clip.</li>\n<li>Drop the drive folder link in the team chat.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> 10 labeled clips in the shared drive + a 10-row index in the tracker.\n<strong>Done when:</strong> A teammate can find and download &quot;the leaderboard clip&quot; from the tracker alone, without asking you.\n<strong>Depends on:</strong> —</p>\n"
