       "time": "45–60 min",
       "dep": null,
       "html": "<p><strong>Why:</strong> Three lists of 20 gives the team 60 warm contacts and 15 honest first messages this week — that&#39;s more likely to produce our first activated users than anything the algorithm does today.\n<strong>Where:</strong> Your own contacts (WhatsApp/Messages/DMs) + the tracker <code>Outreach</code> tab.\n<strong>Tools:</strong> Phone, <code>buzzend-marketing/12-community/community-playbook.md</code> (first-message template — tone reference only), CTA discipline from template #6 in <code>buzzend-marketing/16-templates/content-templates.md</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>List 20 real contacts in the <code>Outreach</code> tab with a &quot;why Buzzend fits them&quot; column — think of who complains about gym prices, does home workouts, or is competitive in the group chat.</li>\n<li>Pick today&#39;s 5 and write each message from scratch in your voice: personal first line about them, one plain sentence on Buzzend (&quot;the phone camera counts your reps out loud&quot;), one honest ask.</li>\n<li>The ask: &quot;try it and tell me honestly what confused you&quot; — never beg for downloads, never ask for ratings. If two messages look alike, rewrite one.</li>\n<li>Include the right store link from <code>sprint/config.js</code> for their phone. One ask per message.</li>\n<li>Send all 5 and watch for replies during your engagement windows.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> 20-contact list + 5 personalized messages sent.\n<strong>Done when:</strong> 5 visibly-different messages are out and the 20 rows exist for the coming days.\n<strong>Depends on:</strong> —</p>\n"
