       "dep": null,
       "html": "<p><strong>Why:</strong> Day 14&#39;s readout compares Day 1 → Day 8 → today. If today&#39;s row is missing or half-filled, the readout becomes guesswork on the day it matters most.\n<strong>Where:</strong> Growth Tracker, App Store Connect, Play Console (ask Gaurab for the Android numbers if his session is fresher), each social app.\n<strong>Tools:</strong> Google Sheets, App Store Connect login, phone.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Fill today&#39;s <code>Daily Numbers</code> row completely: iOS installs, Android installs, new followers (total), challenge joins, notes — exact numbers, no blanks.</li>\n<li>In <code>Store-iOS</code>, add today&#39;s Impressions, Product Page Views, Conversion Rate, Downloads next to the Day-1 baseline columns so the delta is visible in one glance.</li>\n<li>Below the row, write a 3-line trend note in the sheet: (a) installs vs baseline — up/flat/down and by how much, (b) which platform is sending the most store visits, (c) the one number that worries you.</li>\n<li>Post the 3 lines in the team chat so Day 12–13 decisions use them.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> Complete mid-sprint row + 3-line trend note in the tracker and team chat.\n<strong>Done when:</strong> Gaurab and Riya have read the trend note and every cell in today&#39;s row has a number.\n<strong>Depends on:</strong> —</p>\n"
