       "pri": "🔥",
       "title": "Repost the strongest TikTok in a new time slot and log the timing experiment",
       "time": "75–90 min",
       "dep": null,
       "html": "<p><strong>Why:</strong> Every post so far went out at the fixed evening slot. We&#39;ve never tested whether a different hour reaches a different (maybe bigger) slice of our audience. Reposting our proven video at a new time isolates timing as the only variable — a clean, free experiment.\n<strong>Where:</strong> TikTok app + Growth Tracker <code>Experiments</code> tab.\n<strong>Tools:</strong> Android phone, TikTok, Growth Tracker, <code>buzzend-marketing/11-publishing/publishing-playbook.md</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>In the tracker, find the TikTok with the most link taps / store-visit correlation so far (winner rule — not likes). Note exactly when it was originally posted.</li>\n<li>Open TikTok analytics → Followers → most-active hours. Pick the strongest activity window we have NEVER posted in (the playbook&#39;s starting slot was 18:00–21:00 — so this is probably a morning or midday window).</li>\n<li>Repost the same video as a new post: same file, same caption, same hashtags, same cover frame, same pinned comment (&quot;It&#39;s Buzzend — App Store &amp; Google Play 🔗 in bio&quot;, links from <code>sprint/config.js</code> via the bio page). Time is the ONLY thing that changes.</li>\n<li>Stay 30–60 min after posting replying to comments, same as the original got.</li>\n<li>Log it in <code>Experiments</code> using template #13 from <code>buzzend-marketing/16-templates/planning-templates.md</code>: Hypothesis (&quot;We believe posting at [new slot] will improve views + link taps because our followers are most active then&quot;), the ONE variable (posting time), Control (original post + its first-72h numbers), Metric (views, link taps, store visits in 72h), Review date = Day 15.</li>\n<li>Check Avinaya&#39;s experiment row from this morning — confirm you two used different videos.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> Repost live at the new slot + one complete <code>Experiments</code> row with a Day-15 review date.\n<strong>Done when:</strong> Both experiment rows sit in the tab, each with exactly one variable and a review date.\n<strong>Depends on:</strong> —</p>\n"
