       "time": "45–60 min",
       "dep": null,
       "html": "<p><strong>Why:</strong> We publish from iPhones and check on iPhones. Half our audience watches on Android, where compression, cropping, and caption size behave differently. Fifteen minutes of watching like a user catches problems no analytics dashboard will ever show.\n<strong>Where:</strong> Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, Facebook apps on your Android device.\n<strong>Tools:</strong> Android phone, Growth Tracker <code>Notes</code> (or a <code>Content</code> tab row per post).</p>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Open our profile on each platform on your Android phone and play every published video (Reels #1–3, the challenge announcement, the carousel, today&#39;s repost) at normal brightness, no headphones.</li>\n<li>For each, check: does it play smoothly, is the burned-in caption text readable on a small screen, does the counter number on screen stay legible, is anything important cropped by the UI (buttons, captions, progress bar)?</li>\n<li>Check the carousel: do all slides render sharp, or did compression blur the text?</li>\n<li>Log every issue in the tracker as a future-edit note, e.g. &quot;caption font too small on 6.1-inch screens — go bigger from now on&quot; or &quot;counter sits under the TikTok caption zone — keep it upper-third&quot;.</li>\n<li>Turn the notes into a short &quot;Android checks&quot; list and paste it into the team chat — Riya and Avinaya apply it to every future edit (and Day 15&#39;s SOP will absorb it).</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> Per-post check notes in the tracker + the &quot;Android checks&quot; list in team chat.\n<strong>Done when:</strong> Every published video has been watched on Android and has a ✓ or a written fix note.\n<strong>Depends on:</strong> —</p>\n"
