       "time": "90–110 min",
       "dep": null,
       "html": "<p><strong>Why:</strong> The 7-Day Squat Starter challenge is our best conversion tool, and weekends are when beginners actually have time to start. A named, personal invite converts many times better than any broadcast — and we already know exactly who cares: they told us in the comments and DMs.\n<strong>Where:</strong> Instagram + TikTok (comments/DM threads), Growth Tracker <code>Outreach</code> tab.\n<strong>Tools:</strong> Phone, Growth Tracker, <code>buzzend-marketing/12-community/community-playbook.md</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Plan 2 countdown stories — one for Saturday, one for Sunday: story 1 = &quot;Weekend plan: join the 7-Day Squat Starter — day 1 is just 10 squats, the camera counts them&quot; with the countdown/poll sticker; story 2 = a real leaderboard moment or participant shout-out (first names only, with permission) + &quot;still time to join&quot;. Write the exact text for both in the tracker and note the posting times (Saturday morning, Sunday morning).</li>\n<li>Build the invite list: scroll every post&#39;s comments, our DM inbox, and repeat likers from this sprint. List every person who commented, DM&#39;d, or has liked us repeatedly — cap at 20. Real engagers only; nobody we&#39;ve never interacted with.</li>\n<li>Write each invite INDIVIDUALLY, using their name and referencing what they actually said or did (&quot;You asked if the counter works in a small room — it does, and the squat challenge is the easiest way to see it&quot;). Include the 3 join steps: download Buzzend (link from <code>sprint/config.js</code> in our bio) → open Discover → join &quot;7-Day Squat Starter&quot;. End with a question, not a pitch.</li>\n<li>Deliver each invite where the relationship already exists: reply in the DM thread if there is one, otherwise reply to their comment. No cold promo DMs to people who only liked once — the community playbook bans unsolicited promo DMs, and one warm invite beats five awkward ones.</li>\n<li>Log every invite in the <code>Outreach</code> tab: name, platform, what they engaged with, sent date, reply (fill in as they come).</li>\n<li>Absolute rule: no copy-paste blast. If two invites read identical, rewrite one.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> 2 written weekend stories (text + times) + up to 20 logged personal invites.\n<strong>Done when:</strong> Every row in the invite list shows a personalized message sent (or a reason skipped), and both story texts are ready to post.\n<strong>Depends on:</strong> —</p>\n"
