       "html": "<p><strong>Why:</strong> Review count is a store ranking factor, and the only reviews worth having come from people who genuinely use Buzzend. Someone who has done 3+ days of counted squats has an honest opinion — asking them isn&#39;t begging, it&#39;s giving them a place to say it.\n<strong>Where:</strong> Buzzend app (7-Day Squat Starter leaderboard) + wherever we already talk to each person (DM thread, comment thread), Growth Tracker.\n<strong>Tools:</strong> Phone, Growth Tracker <code>Outreach</code> tab, <code>buzzend-marketing/12-community/community-playbook.md</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Open the 7-Day Squat Starter leaderboard and list everyone who has completed 3+ days of camera-counted workouts — these are our genuine, engaged users.</li>\n<li>Cross-check the list against Riya&#39;s Day-12 invite log and our DM/comment history: pick up to 5 people we already have a real interaction with. Someone we&#39;ve never spoken to gets a warm conversation first, not a review ask — never ask strangers.</li>\n<li>Message each one individually, by name, referencing their actual progress (&quot;Day 4 of the squat challenge — you&#39;re ahead of most of us&quot;). The ask, in your own words each time: &quot;If you have 2 minutes, an honest review on the store would genuinely help a 3-person team. Whatever you really think.&quot;</li>\n<li>Hard rules: no incentive of any kind, no asking for 5 stars or &quot;positive&quot; reviews, no follow-up nagging if they don&#39;t do it. One honest ask, then let it go. If anyone already left a review, thank them instead (Avinaya is replying to reviews today — coordinate).</li>\n<li>Note today&#39;s review count on both stores in the tracker (<code>Store-iOS</code>/<code>Store-Android</code>) and add a &quot;review asks sent&quot; row in <code>Outreach</code>: name, day count in challenge, date asked. Check the delta on Day 15.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> Up to 5 individual, honest review asks sent + review-count baseline row in the tracker.\n<strong>Done when:</strong> Every ask is logged with a name and a reason (&quot;3+ challenge days, existing DM thread&quot;), and today&#39;s review counts are recorded.\n<strong>Depends on:</strong> Riya · Day 12 · Task 1 (her invite log tells you who&#39;s already in a warm thread).</p>\n"
