       "html": "<p><strong>Why:</strong> This is the payoff of every number we logged since Day 1. The readout is what we show the founders, what Day 15&#39;s retro runs on, and what next sprint&#39;s goals come from. It&#39;s assembly, not analysis theater: every figure already sits in the tracker — your job is to line them up so they speak.\n<strong>Where:</strong> New file <code>buzzend-marketing/14-weekly-reports/sprint-readout.md</code> (beside Day 11&#39;s <code>sprint-feedback.md</code>), Growth Tracker.\n<strong>Tools:</strong> Code editor, Growth Tracker, <code>buzzend-marketing/16-templates/planning-templates.md</code> (templates #11 and #12 as skeletons), <code>buzzend-marketing/13-analytics/metrics-for-beginners.md</code> if any term feels shaky.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Create <code>buzzend-marketing/14-weekly-reports/sprint-readout.md</code>. Structure it with template #11&#39;s &quot;numbers first, adjectives never&quot; spirit, expanded to 15 days.</li>\n<li><strong>Installs:</strong> Day-1 baseline vs today, both stores, from <code>Daily Numbers</code>. Absolute numbers and the delta.</li>\n<li><strong>Store conversion:</strong> conversion rate before/after each change we made — Day-2 metadata update, Day-10 audit — from <code>Store-iOS</code>/<code>Store-Android</code>. One line per change: date, what changed, conversion before → after.</li>\n<li><strong>Social:</strong> per platform (Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, Facebook): followers Day 1 → today, total reach, best post with its numbers, engagement. From the <code>Social</code> tab.</li>\n<li><strong>Challenge:</strong> 7-Day Squat Starter — total joins, day-5+ actives, the retention figure from yesterday&#39;s snapshot (quote its source honestly, proxy or console).</li>\n<li><strong>Outreach:</strong> the funnel from the <code>Outreach</code> tab: creator messages sent → replies → collabs in motion; plus Riya&#39;s personal invites and UGC asks with their statuses.</li>\n<li><strong>Experiments:</strong> both Day-12 rows (hook re-cut, timing repost) — numbers so far, control vs variant. Mark them &quot;verdict on Day 15&quot; — the 72h window closes tomorrow; do NOT call a winner early.</li>\n<li>End with <strong>&quot;3 things the numbers prove&quot;</strong> — three one-sentence claims, each pointing at its number. If a claim needs an adjective to sound true, it isn&#39;t proven; pick another.</li>\n<li>Rule check before saving: only numbers already in the tracker. If you catch yourself wanting a metric we never logged, write &quot;not tracked this sprint&quot; — do not go build new tooling today.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> <code>buzzend-marketing/14-weekly-reports/sprint-readout.md</code>, complete with all six sections + the three proofs.\n<strong>Done when:</strong> Someone who ignored the sprint entirely could read it in 5 minutes and repeat the three proofs back to you.\n<strong>Depends on:</strong> —</p>\n"
