       "dep": "Avinaya · Day 15 · Task 1 (the experiment verdicts set the SOP's posting times — draft everything else first).",
       "html": "<p><strong>Why:</strong> &quot;End the 15 days with a repeatable process&quot; was the sprint&#39;s stated goal from day one. The playbooks say how things SHOULD work; this SOP records how they ACTUALLY worked for us — who did what, at what time, with which tools — so next sprint (or a new person) runs week one without re-learning anything.\n<strong>Where:</strong> New file <code>buzzend-marketing/15-team-workflow/publishing-sop.md</code>.\n<strong>Tools:</strong> Code editor, Growth Tracker, <code>buzzend-marketing/15-team-workflow/production-pipeline.md</code>, <code>buzzend-marketing/16-templates/workflow-templates.md</code> (checklist #8), your Day-12 &quot;Android checks&quot; list.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Create <code>buzzend-marketing/15-team-workflow/publishing-sop.md</code>. Open with one line: &quot;This is what we ACTUALLY did for 15 days — not theory. Update it whenever reality changes.&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>Roles as they really settled:</strong> who recorded, who edited, who published, who replied to comments — by name (Avinaya/Gaurab/Riya), with the real handoffs (e.g. edit → Avinaya&#39;s approval pass → publish). Where reality differed from <code>production-pipeline.md</code>&#39;s 14 stages, write what we did and why it worked.</li>\n<li><strong>Tools:</strong> the exact tools we used at each stage (recording phones, editor, Canva, the consoles, the Growth Tracker tabs) — the real list, not a wish list.</li>\n<li><strong>Times:</strong> the posting times we actually used per platform, updated with the Day-12 timing-experiment verdict (get it from Avinaya after the retro — if the new slot WON, the SOP ships with the new slot).</li>\n<li><strong>The per-post checklist:</strong> paste checklist #8 from <code>workflow-templates.md</code> and extend it with what the sprint taught us — your Android device checks from Day 12, the caption-legibility rule, the link-tap test, the one-CTA rule.</li>\n<li><strong>The weekly loop:</strong> what a normal week looks like (batch-film day, publish slots, Friday numbers + outreach), condensed from how our 15 days actually flowed.</li>\n<li>Keep the whole thing under 2 pages — an SOP nobody reads is decoration. Link it from the tracker and in team chat.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> <code>buzzend-marketing/15-team-workflow/publishing-sop.md</code> — the sprint&#39;s repeatable-process deliverable.\n<strong>Done when:</strong> A newcomer could publish Monday&#39;s post correctly using only this doc and the files it links.\n<strong>Depends on:</strong> Avinaya · Day 15 · Task 1 (the experiment verdicts set the SOP&#39;s posting times — draft everything else first).</p>\n"
